<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Hotai limit up on listing debut.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Hotai limit up on listing debut.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's newly listed Hotai Motor soared limit-up in late session with one ceremonial order, or 1,000 shares, traded during its stock market debut on Tuesday.</p>
<p>With 25 minutes left, Hotai was up the daily seven-percent limit or T$3.50 to T$56.</p>
<p>Brokers characterised the rise as a typical honeymoon bounce.</p>
<p>&quot;The fact that only one order of shares has been traded means shareholders are optimistic about the company's outlook and expect the listing to benefit the company,&quot; said Lin Long-hsien, analyst for United Securities.  </p>
<p>Hotai is the distributor in Taiwan for Japan's Toyota Motor.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
